  "现状影像、地形、范围、剖面与来源": "Recent imagery, terrain, areas, profiles and sources",
  "局地 4 期真彩和 DSM 口径均可核对；本包有效范围和分辨率不替代目录中的区域DEM、季节影像、历史波段及原范围。": "The four local true-color scenes and DSM basis are inspectable. The bundle does not replace the regional DEM, seasonal imagery, historical bands or extents in the source catalog.",
  "外围湖及呼和系列": "Peripheral lakes and Huhe series",
  "WF1 是新增独立月序列。东池、北小湖先以少数单景落图，已有 N2 和呼和、其他外围系列沿用原对象ID与固定窗。": "WF1 is an additional monthly series. East Pond and North Lakelet begin with selected scenes. Existing N2, Huhe and other series keep their original IDs and fixed windows.",
  "早期图档及历史语境": "Early maps and historical context",
  "历史事件和图档来源保留；早期图档不拿来代替月度像元岸线。": "Retain historical events and provenance. Early maps do not replace monthly pixel-based shorelines.",
  "场地、建筑、通达与条件方案": "Site, buildings, access and conditional scenarios",
  "条件管理方案、入口与路线须保留但按原情景性质展现；不与西北坡水文学三情景混用。": "Retain conditional management, entrances and routes as scenarios. Do not combine them with the three Northwest Slope hydrology scenarios.",
  "道路／地名／地形参照及质量": "Roads, names, terrain references and quality",
  "使用现有上下文、精简后道路；不把 OSM 当工程设施台账，把道路底图当参照。": "Use existing context and simplified roads. OSM is a reference basemap, not an engineering inventory.",
  "其他冻结分析、数据质量与索引": "Other archived analyses, quality records and indexes",
  "与目录的源文件、筛选方法、口径和哈希一同保留。设计可以决定优先级，但不可静默省略有作用的结论或把数据标成不存在。": "Keep the source files, screening methods, definitions and hashes. Presentation can prioritize findings without silently omitting material evidence or marking present data missing.",
  "证据联动、图文和报告档案": "Linked evidence, illustrated text and reports",
  "保留观察、模型、未知边界和引用关系；图例、叙事排布、交互可重设计。报告历史需以目录保持可追溯。": "Preserve observations, models, uncertainties and citations. Legend, narrative and interactions may be redesigned. Keep report history traceable through the catalog.",
  "原视图控件／展示脚本": "Original controls and presentation scripts",
  "不冻结窗口布局、控件、镜头、色彩、图形、渲染器或动作设计；切换不得改变科学输入。": "Layout, controls, cameras, colors, graphics, renderer and motion are not scientific inputs. Changing them must not change the evidence.",
